  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "open",
      "from": 0,
      "frames": 600,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "AI agents have become remarkable writing partners.",
          "src": "vo/open-0.mp3",
          "at": 24,
          "end": 125,
          "clipFrom": 24
        },
        {
          "text": "In a code editor, they read a whole project, make precise edits, and check their own work.",
          "src": "vo/open-1.mp3",
          "at": 135,
          "end": 323,
          "clipFrom": 135
        },
        {
          "text": "But most of the writing that matters doesn't live in a code editor.",
          "src": "vo/open-2.mp3",
          "at": 351,
          "end": 473,
          "clipFrom": 351
        },
        {
          "text": "It lives on the page.",
          "src": "vo/open-3.mp3",
          "at": 484,
          "end": 546,
          "clipFrom": 484
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "title",
      "from": 600,
      "frames": 195,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "This is Inline.",
          "src": "vo/title-0.mp3",
          "at": 27,
          "end": 82,
          "clipFrom": 27
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "idea",
      "from": 795,
      "frames": 660,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Inline is a paginated document editor with Claude Code and Codex built in.",
          "src": "vo/idea-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 184,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "The agent works on the same page you do, through more than forty document tools.",
          "src": "vo/idea-1.mp3",
          "at": 194,
          "end": 348,
          "clipFrom": 194
        },
        {
          "text": "And every edit it makes is a suggestion you can review.",
          "src": "vo/idea-2.mp3",
          "at": 358,
          "end": 473,
          "clipFrom": 358
        },
        {
          "text": "It's free, and open source.",
          "src": "vo/idea-3.mp3",
          "at": 484,
          "end": 558,
          "clipFrom": 484
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "desktop",
      "from": 1455,
      "frames": 360,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "It runs as a desktop app on Mac, Windows, and Linux, with everything included.",
          "src": "vo/desktop-0.mp3",
          "at": 24,
          "end": 202,
          "clipFrom": 24
        },
        {
          "text": "Let's open a real account.",
          "src": "vo/desktop-1.mp3",
          "at": 212,
          "end": 274,
          "clipFrom": 212
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "home",
      "from": 1815,
      "frames": 660,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "This is home.",
          "src": "vo/home-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 56,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "Documents live in color-coded folders, with live previews of their pages.",
          "src": "vo/home-1.mp3",
          "at": 67,
          "end": 225,
          "clipFrom": 67
        },
        {
          "text": "Templates cover essays, MLA papers, reports, résumés and more.",
          "src": "vo/home-2.mp3",
          "at": 236,
          "end": 406,
          "clipFrom": 236
        },
        {
          "text": "And search finds any document in a keystroke.",
          "src": "vo/home-3.mp3",
          "at": 417,
          "end": 522,
          "clipFrom": 417
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "editor",
      "from": 2475,
      "frames": 660,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Open a thesis proposal and you get real pages.",
          "src": "vo/editor-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 128,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "A live table of contents, citations, LaTeX equations, tables and figures, with headers and page numbers.",
          "src": "vo/editor-1.mp3",
          "at": 139,
          "end": 372,
          "clipFrom": 139
        },
        {
          "text": "Everything you'd expect from a word processor.",
          "src": "vo/editor-2.mp3",
          "at": 382,
          "end": 471,
          "clipFrom": 382
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "chat",
      "from": 3135,
      "frames": 1020,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Press Command J, and Claude joins you.",
          "src": "vo/chat-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 112,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "Ask it to tighten the introduction.",
          "src": "vo/chat-1.mp3",
          "at": 122,
          "end": 199,
          "clipFrom": 122
        },
        {
          "text": "Claude reads the document and edits the page directly.",
          "src": "vo/chat-2.mp3",
          "at": 209,
          "end": 320,
          "clipFrom": 209
        },
        {
          "text": "Every change appears as a tracked suggestion: deletions struck through, additions highlighted.",
          "src": "vo/chat-3.mp3",
          "at": 330,
          "end": 527,
          "clipFrom": 330
        },
        {
          "text": "It even noticed a citation that doesn't match its source.",
          "src": "vo/chat-4.mp3",
          "at": 538,
          "end": 646,
          "clipFrom": 538
        },
        {
          "text": "Keep what you like and undo the rest, one change at a time, or all at once.",
          "src": "vo/chat-5.mp3",
          "at": 656,
          "end": 829,
          "clipFrom": 656
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "select",
      "from": 4155,
      "frames": 660,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Select a passage and press Command L to ask about just that part.",
          "src": "vo/select-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 164,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "Here, Claude checks the claim against the paper, finds the right hurricane, and rewrites the sentence, with its sources.",
          "src": "vo/select-1.mp3",
          "at": 175,
          "end": 417,
          "clipFrom": 175
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "comments",
      "from": 4815,
      "frames": 600,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Comments work the way you'd expect.",
          "src": "vo/comments-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 85,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "My advisor left three.",
          "src": "vo/comments-1.mp3",
          "at": 96,
          "end": 163,
          "clipFrom": 96
        },
        {
          "text": "Ask Claude to address them, and it fixes each one in the text, replies in the thread, and resolves it.",
          "src": "vo/comments-2.mp3",
          "at": 173,
          "end": 382,
          "clipFrom": 173
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "history",
      "from": 5415,
      "frames": 420,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Save named versions as you go, and open any earlier draft to compare it or restore it.",
          "src": "vo/history-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 200,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "Every reply from the agent leaves a restore checkpoint, too.",
          "src": "vo/history-1.mp3",
          "at": 211,
          "end": 326,
          "clipFrom": 211
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "providers",
      "from": 5835,
      "frames": 390,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Prefer Codex?",
          "src": "vo/providers-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 61,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "Switch providers or models in the middle of a conversation.",
          "src": "vo/providers-1.mp3",
          "at": 72,
          "end": 182,
          "clipFrom": 72
        },
        {
          "text": "The next model picks up the same transcript, and the same document.",
          "src": "vo/providers-2.mp3",
          "at": 193,
          "end": 313,
          "clipFrom": 193
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "canvas",
      "from": 6225,
      "frames": 510,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "When the layout is part of the message, use a Canvas.",
          "src": "vo/canvas-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 131,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "The agent designs editable pages with columns, color, and type, and you can still click in and change any word.",
          "src": "vo/canvas-1.mp3",
          "at": 141,
          "end": 379,
          "clipFrom": 141
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pdf",
      "from": 6735,
      "frames": 690,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Import a PDF, and Inline matches its page size, fonts, and margins.",
          "src": "vo/pdf-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 184,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Claude rebuilds each page as editable text, with equations in LaTeX, and checks its work against the original, side by side.",
          "src": "vo/pdf-1.mp3",
          "at": 194,
          "end": 470,
          "clipFrom": 194
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "organize",
      "from": 7425,
      "frames": 450,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Back home, Organize with AI files everything into folders in seconds.",
          "src": "vo/organize-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 181,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "It reads only titles and first lines, so it barely touches your usage.",
          "src": "vo/organize-1.mp3",
          "at": 192,
          "end": 345,
          "clipFrom": 192
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "files",
      "from": 7875,
      "frames": 540,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Your documents stay yours.",
          "src": "vo/files-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 90,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "Inline keeps a Word copy of every one in a folder on your computer, exports to PDF, Markdown and more, and brings in your whole Google Drive from a single zip.",
          "src": "vo/files-1.mp3",
          "at": 101,
          "end": 434,
          "clipFrom": 101
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mcp",
      "from": 8415,
      "frames": 570,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And because Inline speaks MCP, Claude Code in your terminal can work on your documents too.",
          "src": "vo/mcp-0.mp3",
          "at": 18,
          "end": 210,
          "clipFrom": 18
        },
        {
          "text": "Ask from the command line, and watch the edit land on the page.",
          "src": "vo/mcp-1.mp3",
          "at": 221,
          "end": 343,
          "clipFrom": 221
        }
      ]
    },
